body:

<div id="page-body-countdown-container"></div>

<img src="/current/starship-pad-boat.jpg" alt="Photo of the SpaceX Starship on the pad, with a boat in the foreground" style="display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; margin-top: 5px; margin-bottom: 20px;">

Join Star Fleet for the first-ever flight of a fully-resuable orbital rocket, and the first ever landing attempt of both the Starship upper stage and the V3 version of the Super Heavy booster!
The launch is ** *No Earlier Than* Mid-November **, and we'll be out there to view it!
In addition, we'll run a separate trip at a discount to view the landing, from the very same close-up spot (hazard zones allowing, which are currently to-be-confirmed but should be known before we release tickets for it).

Our planned [Starship launch and landing viewing location at the mouth of the South Bay](https://www.google.com/maps/search/26.052814,+-97.185356), approximately 4 miles / 6.5 km from the launch site with a direct line of sight across the water, provides some of the closest and clearest views of the pad, rocket, liftoff, booster landing and ship landing available to the public.
Unlike the location where most other vessels anchor, this offers a closer and clearer sightline, and has calmer, less busy waters without the need to constantly jockey for position.


**LATEST LAUNCH UPDATE**:
As of *Thursday November 5*, SpaceX has successfully static fired both Booster and Ship, and are preparing for rollout to the pad.
The current earliest No Earlier Than (NET) date is NET November 13 per aviation advisories and other sources, with the major pacing item believed to be regulatory approval at the moment, with later in mid-November currently believed to be the most likely time.
We are currently closely monitoring our sources for solid confirmation of a specific date, and will open up tickets as soon as we have one!
In the meantime, we encourage you to join our WhatsApp community, where we and our members provide folks with insider updates we can't share with the general public.
Looking forward to seeing you all there!

*We have **[a Whats App community](INSERT_URL_1) that we highly recommend you join**, with channels for announcements, insider launch updates, discussion, questions and more!
We also use it for early tickets, special community events and more!
You can also follow our [Twitter](https://twitter.com/StarFleetTours), [Instagram](https://instagram.com/starfleettours/) and [Facebook](https://www.facebook.com/starfleettours/) for announcements and updates.
Thanks!*

